      "side": 1,
      "message": "`--changed-lines` corrupts multi-line statements. Commit `return \"a\"` / `+ \"b\"` / `+ \"c\";` on three lines, change only `+ \"b\"` to `+ \"B\"`, run `--changed-lines HEAD --write`: the unchanged `+ \"c\";` line gets merged onto the edited line. The region passed to the formatter ends at the start of the *next* line, so formatting that fragment as a `K_COMPILATION_UNIT` pulls the following line in (and can rewrite its indentation). `--check` flags it, then `--write` writes broken Java. The region should end at the end of the last changed line, not the start of the next. Please fix and add a regression test -- editing one line inside a multi-line statement isn\u0027t covered today.",
      "isAi": true,
